  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f(1)=-2$ and $f^{\\prime}(x) \\geq 4.2$ for $1 \\leq x \\leq 6$. The possible value of $f(6)$ lies in the interval :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "C7bu0",
      "text": "\n$[15,19)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "yydPL",
      "text": "\n $(-\\infty, 12)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "RUjl6",
      "text": "\n$[12,15)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "a7kB3",
      "text": "\n$[19, \\infty)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $f(1)=-2$ and $f^{\\prime}(x) \\geq 4.2$ for $1 \\leq x \\leq 6$\nConsider $f^{\\prime}(x)=\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}$ $\\Rightarrow f(x+h)-f(x)=f^{\\prime}(x) \\cdot h \\geq(4.2) h$\nSo, $f(x+h) \\geq f(x)+(4.2) h$\nput $x=1$ and $h=5$, we get\n$f(6) \\geq f(1)+5(4.2) \\Rightarrow f(6) \\geq 19$\nHence $f(6)$ lies in $[19, \\infty)$",
    "image": null
  },
